  "worked_solution": "Let's recall some of the basic properties of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x:$\n\n- The minimum value is $-1,$ and the maximum value is $1.$\n\n- The period of the function is $2\\pi .$\n\n- Its zeros occur at $x=0,\\pm \\pi ,\\pm 2\\pi ,….$\n\n- Its maximum values occur at $…,-\\frac{3\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2},…$\n\n- Its minimum values occur at $…,-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{3\\pi }{2},…$\n\nOf the given functions, the only one that has all of these properties is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14254255/assets/1dfe4444da1a8f30db08c90de8efecbe1214125b1cfbf49c2ae8681edf3d10db.png)",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
